      {
        "id": 177704,
        "name": "LewdDolphin21",
        "username": "LewdDolphin21",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lewddolphin21/{size}/1893_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-07-07T03:20:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Because it doesn't have you play it next to a target, even though it copies that wording. &nbsp;Apparently copying the text counts as the card entering play, but not as the card being played/put into play.</p>\n<p>Which makes no sense.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Well, it sort of does. The card has entered play, i.e. it was played. So it would ignore the effects that say \"Play this card next to a target,\" because it has already been played. It's different than the effects that say \"When this card enters play,\" because it is still in the process of entering play, but has already been played.</p>\n<p>What we really need is an Ongoing card that says something like \"When this card enters play, place it next to a target\" to see what Uh Yeah, I'm That Guy does.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:01:45.093Z",
